  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating an evidence-base for developing and evaluating interventions to reduce unsustainable bushmeat hunting in Central Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to advance our understanding of the effectiveness of efforts that address the impact of the commercial bushmeat trade by improving the tools and evidence available to design and evaluate interventions. Specific activities include: (1) development of an open-access database of bushmeat hunting, trade and consumption, and interventions; (2) development of performance indicators and methods to better monitor bushmeat use at local, national, and regional-levels; and (3) participation and technical assistance in regional and international policy meetings to promote the available evidence on the effectiveness of relevant bushmeat law and policy.</narrative>
  </description>
